-   - For every voxel value $v$ in the input grid:
-     - If $v < min_{iso}$, set $v \leftarrow min_{iso}$ [S2, S4].
-     - If $v > max_{iso}$, set $v \leftarrow max_{iso}$ [S2, S4].
-   - This clamping increases the likelihood of zero-variance regions outside the range of interest, allowing them to be consolidated into the tree [S2, S4]. Values within the range remain unchanged, preserving lossless quality for those isosurfaces [S2, S4].
