-## Subtopics
-
-### Lossless Consolidation
-The core mechanism of merging zero-variance voxels. Choose this when data has large uniform regions and full fidelity is required.
-
-### Iso-Range Clamping
-A preprocessing step to enhance compression by reducing value spread. Choose this when only a specific subset of isosurfaces is needed for rendering.
-
-### Lossy Variance Thresholding
-Aggressive merging of low-variance regions. Choose this for very large, gradually varying datasets where minor quantization errors are acceptable.
+- **Clamping Artifacts:** Clamping outside the range of interest is lossless *only* for isosurfaces within that range [S2, S4]. Isosurfaces outside the range are altered [S2, S4].
 
